  "note": "Merowe Dam’s west and east embankments, central spillway with twelve low sluices and two surface gates, angled intake dam, ten domed turbine housings, powerhouse and immediate service structures. Absolute mean-sea-level placement fixes the modeled crest at 303 m. The design full pool is 300 m. With the retained PMTiles shorelines and standard Terrarium terrain, the runtime water sampler gives 252.43–271.86 m in central reservoir tiles and 250.22–255.31 m in the tailwater. Changing the terrain provider does not move the dam. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
